@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; A point that folds onto a line lands on the paper of that line (decisions/toward-names-the-side-that-stays).
; The circle about .q through .d meets --ef at (1/2, 5/6) and at (1/2, -1/2);
; the second lies beside the paper, so the fold that would take .d there
; drops out at the moved-material stage, and the other remains.

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --ef
.q = free on --da from .a at 1/6
fold (map .d onto --ef through .q) (moving .d)

; assert steps = 1
; assert .d = (1/2, 5/6)
